The features folder contains documentation files that define key project functionalities and components. The contribute.md file outlines how players can submit data to the Shattered Archive project, while questbot.md describes automation features for quest cycles. The user-equipment.md and user-library.md files document character equipment tracking and a React component structure respectively, all serving as reference materials for developers and contributors working on the project's core systems. library-sync.md (2026-08) is the player-facing companion to user-library.md, covering Library-content cloud sync (parchment/notes/books) across web, mobile, and the site's "My Writings" page, including how per-account encryption at rest works in plain terms. organizations.md (2026-08) documents the Organizations feature, now fully COMPLETE (Phase 2, all 7 steps, live-verified end to end across web/game-client/mobile) — kingdoms/clans/religions/friend groups, playing as a character with one-org-per-category (auto-leave on a same-category move), account-level admin roles for cross-org access, invites vs. join requests, leave/remove vs. account-wide bans, shared org content in nested folders, an audit log, append-only revision history with web-only revert, per-group envelope-key encryption with rotation on any access loss. Org management (create/invite/roles/bans) and revision history/audit stay website-only by design; browsing + role-gated content editing works on all three clients (Library → Organizations on web, a Library tab on game-client, a More-menu screen on mobile).
